MARS(1)                         User Commands                         MARS(1)

NAME
     mars - minimal single-instrument latent-state trading research engine

SYNOPSIS
     make
     make install

     mars fit input.csv model.mars
     mars inspect model.mars
     mars replay input.csv model.mars trades.csv

     mars db-init market.db
     mars eth-update market.db FROM_BLOCK TO_BLOCK [--blocks-only]
     mars eth-export market.db eth_blocks.csv
     mars fred-update market.db SERIES[,SERIES...]
     mars fred-export market.db fred.csv

DESCRIPTION
     mars is a small research engine for fitting, inspecting, and replaying a
     latent-state trading model for one instrument at a time.

     The intended first instrument is CME ES/MES 1-second top-of-book bars.

FILES
     mars.c
          Plain C command entrypoint and argument dispatch.

     mars_api.h
          C-compatible boundary, status codes, constants, and shared POD
          model/data types.

     mars_core.cpp
          C++ orchestration over focused module classes.

     csv.cpp, csv.hpp
          CsvData: load and release market data.

     features.cpp, features.hpp
          FeatureBuilder: construct model features from market rows.

     scale.cpp, scale.hpp
          ScalerOps: fit/apply scalers and build feature matrices.

     hmm.cpp, hmm.hpp
          HmmModel: fit and filter latent states.

     alpha.cpp, alpha.hpp
          AlphaModel: train and apply the sparse alpha model.

     backtest.cpp, backtest.hpp
          Backtester: replay predictions into PnL and trade output.

     model_store.cpp, model_store.hpp
          ModelStore: default config, validation, save, and load.

     report.cpp, report.hpp
          Reporter: stats and model inspection output.

     db.cpp
          SQLite-backed Ethereum and FRED ingestion/export commands.

     README_DB
          DB ingestion usage notes and schema overview.

     Makefile
          Builds and installs mars. DB ingestion links against libcurl and
          sqlite3.

INPUT
     The input CSV schema is:

          ts,bid,ask,bid_sz,ask_sz,volume
          1700000000,5000.00,5000.25,115,103,90

     DB ingestion commands write local SQLite data and export CSV feature
     panels. See README_DB for Ethereum and FRED examples.

COMMANDS
     make
          Build the mars binary.

     make install
          Install mars to PREFIX/bin. PREFIX defaults to /usr/local.

     make install PREFIX=$HOME/.local
          Install mars to $HOME/.local/bin for a user-local setup.
          Ensure $HOME/.local/bin is in PATH to run mars by name.

     mars fit es_1s.csv es.mars
          Fit a model.

     mars inspect es.mars
          Inspect learned latent states and sparse alpha coefficients.

     mars replay es_1s.csv es.mars trades.csv
          Replay or backtest a fitted model.

     mars db-init market.db
          Initialize the local SQLite learning database.

     mars eth-update market.db FROM_BLOCK TO_BLOCK [--blocks-only]
          Fetch Ethereum block and optional transaction data using ETH_RPC_URL.

     mars eth-export market.db eth_blocks.csv
          Export Ethereum block-level learning features.

     mars fred-update market.db SERIES[,SERIES...]
          Fetch FRED observations using FRED_API_KEY.

     mars fred-export market.db fred.csv
          Export stored FRED observations.

DESIGN
     Instrument choice
          ES/MES first, because it is centralized, liquid, tick-discrete,
          high-frequency enough to learn microstructure states, and avoids
          corporate actions, borrow, and fragmented equity NBBO reconstruction.

     Latent states
          Learned by causal diagonal-Gaussian HMM filtering. States are not
          manually named. Inspect state emission means after fitting.

     Alpha
          Regime-interacted elastic net. Rich enough to condition on latent
          regimes; sparse enough to avoid feature proliferation.

     Execution model
          One-unit position in {-1,0,+1}, hard spread guard, cost threshold,
          and validation gate. If validation is not positive after costs, the
          saved model is deployment-disabled with pos_max=0.

     Style
          Single binary, plain Makefile, C command surface, C++ core behind a
          small C ABI, deterministic replay, checked return values, no
          recursion, and bounded inner loops.

STATUS
     This is a research scaffold. It is not a broker adapter, not a live
     execution engine, and not a claim about Renaissance Technologies' actual
     code.
